version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-26'
abstract: >-
  A modular Sankey diagram layout library that separates the combinatorial and
  geometric stages of layout optimisation. Link crossings are reduced by a
  median or barycentre sweep refined with simulated-annealing swaps; node
  coordinates are settled by a one-dimensional spring relaxation with separate
  stiffnesses for edge, node and margin springs; and links are drawn with a
  ribbon geometry built from paired cubic Béziers, which eliminates overlap
  between parallel links. It further supports three clutter-reducing encodings
  that extend the layout itself rather than the renderer: packed paths, which
  merge runs of dummy nodes into a single vertex; totalizing nodes, which gather
  a bundle of links while preserving each link's original endpoints; and hidden
  nodes, which are removed from layer assignment, crossing counts and the spring
  system, and shown instead by markers on the nodes they touch.
keywords:
  - sankey diagram
  - flow visualization
  - graph drawing
  - layout algorithm
